{"id":"n-20261005-bz50vy","category":"finance","display_title":"Mortgage Rates Hit 6%","display_title_he":"שיעורי המשכנתאות הגיעו ל-6 אחוזים","short_summary":"Average five-year fixed mortgage rates in the UK have reached 6% for the first time in three years, as financial markets face rising borrowing costs and global economic uncertainty.","english_level":"C1","words":266,"reading_time":2,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/30_year_fixed_rate_mortgage_average_in_the_United_States.webp/960px-30_year_fixed_rate_mortgage_average_in_the_United_States.webp?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Wikideas1 · CC0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:30_year_fixed_rate_mortgage_average_in_the_United_States.webp"},"sources":[{"name":"BBC News","domain":"bbc.co.uk","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8r4yxpry5e9o","title":"Average five-year mortgage rate hits 6% for first time in three years","published_at":"2026-10-05T09:54:57.000Z"},{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/money/2026/oct/05/five-year-fixed-mortgage-rate-banks-building-societies","title":"Average five-year fixed mortgage rate hits 6% for first time in three years","published_at":"2026-10-05T11:39:37.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-05T09:54:57.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-05T19:22:49.659Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The average interest rate on a new five-year fixed mortgage deal has reached 6% for the first time in three years, according to financial data. This sudden shift means that home buyers and individuals renewing their fixed arrangements face a dramatically altered lending environment. Financial information service Moneyfacts reported that approximately 1,500 mortgage deals priced below 5% have vanished since the beginning of September.","Experts described the current market situation as brutal for borrowers, noting that the average rate on two-year fixed mortgages has climbed to 5.98%. While the Bank of England base rate has remained unchanged since December of last year, international economic uncertainty stemming from the Iran war has driven up government borrowing costs and wholesale funding expenses for banks. Major high street lenders, including Barclays, HSBC, Lloyds Bank, Nationwide, NatWest, Santander, and TSB, implemented multiple rounds of rate increases throughout September.","Rachel Springall, a finance expert at Moneyfacts, explained that the rapid return to three-year highs is disastrous news for individuals who anticipated stabilizing borrowing expenses. The dramatic contraction in the market means that the number of fixed-rate deals priced under 5% has plummeted by 99%, dropping from 1,494 options at the start of September down to just nine choices.","Analysts note that the higher financial burden is already cooling the property sector. Nationwide building society reported that annual house price growth halved in September, while industry representatives indicate that buyers are highly sensitive to these elevated expenses. With more than five million homeowners scheduled to exit their current fixed deals by the end of 2028, experts advise consumers to seek professional guidance and carefully examine available alternatives well in advance."],"facts":[{"fact":"Average interest rate on a new five-year fixed mortgage has hit 6% for the first time in three years.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Average two-year fixed mortgage rate is at 5.98%.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Number of fixed-rate mortgage deals priced below 5% dropped from 1,494 at the start of September to just nine.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Global economic uncertainty and rising government borrowing costs follow the start of the Iran war.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Major high street lenders including Barclays, HSBC, Lloyds, Nationwide, NatWest, Santander, and TSB repeatedly raised fixed rates during September.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Over five million homeowners expect higher monthly mortgage repayments by the end of 2028 according to Bank of England forecasts.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Nationwide building society reported that annual property price growth halved in September.","sources":[2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"average","lemma":"average","pos":"adjective","he":"ממוצע","name":false},{"text":"interest rate","lemma":"interest rate","pos":"compound","he":"שער ריבית","name":false},{"text":"five-year","lemma":"five-year","pos":"adjective","he":"למשך חמש שנים","name":false},{"text":"fixed mortgage","lemma":"fixed mortgage","pos":"compound","he":"משכנתא בריבית קבועה","name":false},{"text":"hit","lemma":"hit","pos":"verb","he":"הגיע ל-","name":false},{"text":"first time","lemma":"first time","pos":"noun","he":"פעם ראשונה","name":false},{"text":"three years","lemma":"three years","pos":"noun","he":"שלוש שנים","name":false},{"text":"financial data","lemma":"financial data","pos":"compound","he":"נתונים פיננסיים","name":false},{"text":"home buyers","lemma":"home buyer","pos":"noun","he":"קוני בתים","name":false},{"text":"individuals","lemma":"individual","pos":"noun","he":"אנשים / פרטים","name":false},{"text":"renewing","lemma":"renew","pos":"verb","he":"מחדשים","name":false},{"text":"fixed arrangements","lemma":"fixed arrangement","pos":"noun","he":"הסדרים קבועים","name":false},{"text":"lending environment","lemma":"lending environment","pos":"compound","he":"סביבת הלוואות","name":false},{"text":"Moneyfacts","lemma":"Moneyfacts","pos":"name","he":"מוניפקטס","name":true},{"text":"approximately","lemma":"approximately","pos":"adverb","he":"בערך","name":false},{"text":"vanished","lemma":"vanish","pos":"verb","he":"נעלמו","name":false},{"text":"beginning of September","lemma":"beginning of September","pos":"noun","he":"תחילת ספטמבר","name":false},{"text":"experts","lemma":"expert","pos":"noun","he":"מומחים","name":fal